==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|whole chebang|whole shebangs|whole shabang}}

===Etymology===
Fixed expression from {{m|en|shebang}},<ref name="wo">{{R:Wordorigins.org|whole_shebang_the|whole shebang, the|Tuesday, February 20, 2007}}</ref><ref name="oed">{{R:OED}}</ref><ref name="tow">[http://www.takeourword.com/TOW193/page2.html Take our Word]</ref> first attested in the United States from the early 1860s, from which time it has increasingly dominated uses of "shebang" itself.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-whole shebang.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|with "the"}} [[everything|Everything]]; the [[entire]] [[thing]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:everything}}
#: {{ux|en|The festival had balloons, flowers, fireworks, performers, and the '''whole shebang'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1863|author=James Bryan|title=A Short Account of the "Mary Ann" Hospital, Grand Gulf, Miss.
|passage=On the third the whole "'''chebang'''" was removed [...]|url=https://www.google.com/books/edition/American_Medical_Times/ipxXAAAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=chebang&pg=PA4&printsec=frontcover}}
#* '''1924''', {{w|Harold Hart Crane}}, letter:<ref name="wo" /><ref name="oed" />
#*: I am growing more and more sick of factions, gossip, jealousies, recriminations, excoriations and the '''whole''' literary '''shee-bang'''.
#* '''2002''', ''Treasure Planet'', directed by {{w|Ron Clements}} and {{w|John Musker}}
#*: Doctor, I'd love to chat. Tea, cake, the '''whole shebang'''. But I've got a ship to launch and you've got your outfit to buff up.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Leo Furey|title=The Long Run|pageurl=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=m_D39nTTNVkC&pg=PA331&dq=%22whole+shebang%22%7C%22whole+shebangs%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=JbIKVZPOA8PVmAXel4H4DQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22whole%20shebang%22%7C%22whole%20shebangs%22&f=false|page=331
|passage=“Food here's pretty good. They don't serve bog juice. Real tea and real coffee. Ice cream, pop, chips. The '''whole shebang'''. Every day's a wingding, brother.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Dave Thompson|title=1000 Songs that Rock Your World|pageurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160310093611/https://books.google.com.au/books?id=U_o9cb5LUn8C&pg=PT208&dq=%22whole+shebang%22%7C%22whole+shebangs%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=JbIKVZPOA8PVmAXel4H4DQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22whole%20shebang%22%7C%22whole%20shebangs%22&f=false|page=209
|passage=Of course, they would win the '''whole shebang''' in 1974, when “Waterloo” [won] (sung in English by Swedes about a Frenchman in Belgium— how much more international can one song get?), but the bitter taste of past failures is not something one forgets...}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Diane Phillips|title=Slow Cooker: The Best Cookbook Ever with More Than 400 Easy-to-Make Recipes|pageurl=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=mW16N47J2-cC&pg=PA305&dq=%22whole+shebang%22%7C%22whole+shebangs%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=JbIKVZPOA8PVmAXel4H4DQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22whole%20shebang%22%7C%22whole%20shebangs%22&f=false|page=305
|passage=The '''whole shebang''' cooks in the slow cooker, which will keep it warm until you are ready to serve it.}}

